<p>Socialist politician Emmanuel Grégoire won the Paris mayoral race on Sunday, succeeding fellow Socialist Anne Hidalgo and extending the left’s control of the French capital. Multiple outlets said he ran on a united left slate that brought together Socialists, Greens and Communists. He beat rival Rachida Dati despite a broad alliance of right-wing and centrist forces backing her candidacy. The municipal runoffs in roughly 1,500 French communes were closely watched as a test of the country’s political balance ahead of the 2027 presidential election. The results painted a mixed picture: Socialists held Paris, Marseille and other large cities; conservatives retained or gained ground elsewhere; Macron’s camp picked up some cities; and the far-right National Rally made gains in smaller and mid-sized towns while failing to capture several headline targets, including Marseille and Toulon. One of its allies did win Nice. For mainstream parties, the outcome suggested that broad local coalitions can still compete effectively in France’s biggest urban centers. For the far right, the night looked more mixed than decisive: leaders pointed to new municipal footholds and argued they still carried national momentum into next year’s presidential contest.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VYoYBJwOlsaqGJFSIwfnAuKeU_x7q2Hi2OGXVshTSz1ANUR5XjB4fnM59Il8R8gAEEO8svfcFYLP0Lrnp8QmYUQAgomLoAlouKbhPUoumCYQGjdgLLp-Fn-MsZkOZzLYQH7TtQfnOJIuzFuly0JhGXdZWAuLHLW2L2X49Gkq2olPJjtlbA' alt='Emmanuel Grégoire holds up the key to Paris City Hall during his victory speech on Place de l&#x27;Hôtel-de-Ville – Esplanade de la Libération on March 22, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Paris margin: Le Monde called Grégoire’s result the united left’s strongest Paris victory since 2001, underscoring just how decisively his coalition performed in the capital.</li><li>Nice shift: The far right’s clearest breakthrough came in Nice, France’s fifth-largest city on the Riviera, giving it a marquee urban win even as it fell short elsewhere.</li><li>Macron allies: Politico reported that President Emmanuel Macron’s Renaissance party won Bordeaux and Annecy, its first two major local victories in these elections.</li><li>Le Havre boost: Former prime minister Edouard Philippe won reelection as mayor of Le Havre, a result Politico said strengthens a possible presidential bid he had tied to that local race.</li><li>Suburb gains: Politico said France Unbowed won several working-class suburbs, advancing a municipal strategy focused on densely populated urban outskirts.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United left coalition: The alliance of Socialists, Greens and Communists cast Grégoire’s win in Paris as proof that a united left can still dominate in large cities, with Le Monde calling it a resounding result and Al Jazeera noting the coalition behind the victory. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/politics/article/2026/03/23/paris-municipal-elections-emmanuel-gregoire-and-the-united-left-achieve-a-resounding-victory_6751716_5.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>National Rally: Party leaders argued that even without winning Marseille, Toulon or Nîmes, gains in smaller and mid-sized towns showed the far right was building a grassroots base ahead of the 2027 presidential election. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/french-municipal-elections-far-right-national-rally-momentum-presidency-marine-le-pen-jordan-bardella/'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Mainstream rivals: Mainstream parties cast the far right’s mixed local performance as encouraging because National Rally failed to turn several top-target cities into statement victories. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-france-municipal-election-results/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li><li>Conservative and centrist bloc: In Paris, right-wing and centrist forces united behind Rachida Dati in an attempt to end the left’s long hold on city hall, but that broad front still lost to Grégoire’s coalition. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/22/paris-mayoral-race-socialist-emmanuel-gregoire-projected-to-win'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/france-leftist-emmanuel-gregoire-becomes-new-mayor-of-paris/a-76478029'>France: Leftist Emmanuel Gregoire becomes new mayor of Paris</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/shorts/RmF3S5nYiiw'>France’s municipal elections : Emmanuel Grégoire elected Paris mayor • FRANCE 24 English</a> - youtube.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crk14m7mjddo'>France&#x27;s Socialists hold on to power in major cities in election boost for mainstream</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-france-municipal-election-results/'>National Rally’s mixed results in French municipal elections offer mainstream rivals hope</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/22/socialist-emmanuel-gregoire-wins-paris-mayoral-race'>Socialist Emmanuel Gregoire wins Paris mayoral race</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3347515/emmanuel-gregoire-becomes-new-mayor-paris-succeeding-fellow-socialist-anne-hidalgo'>Socialist Gregoire becomes Paris mayor in France local elections</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/politics/article/2026/03/23/paris-municipal-elections-emmanuel-gregoire-and-the-united-left-achieve-a-resounding-victory_6751716_5.html'>Paris municipal elections: Emmanuel Grégoire and the united left achieve a resounding victory</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/emmanuel-gregoire-becomes-new-mayor-of-paris-succeeding-fellow-socialist-anne-hidalgo'>Emmanuel Grégoire becomes new mayor of Paris, succeeding fellow Socialist Anne Hidalgo</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/22/world/europe/france-mayor-elections.html'>French Far Right Falls Short of Statement Win in Yardstick Local Races